itle":"Python Control Systems Library - Stochastic Systems","target":"https://python-control.readthedocs.io/en/latest/stochastic.html","line":910},{"title":"Python Control - Discrete Nonlinear Simulation","target":"https://python-control.readthedocs.io/en/0.10.2/examples/simulating_discrete_nonlinear.html","line":911},{"title":"MATLAB idinput Function","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/ident/ref/idinput.html","line":912},{"title":"MATLAB PRBS Input Signals","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/slcontrol/ug/prbs-input-signals.html","line":913},{"title":"MATLAB Generate Adversarial Examples","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ug/generate-adversarial-examples.html","line":914},{"title":"MATLAB Train Robust Network","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ug/train-network-robust-to-adversarial-examples.html","line":915},{"title":"MATLAB verifyNetworkRobustness","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ref/verifynetworkrobustness.html","line":916},{"title":"MATLAB Detect and Mitigate Attacks in Platooning","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/control/ug/detect-and-mitigate-attacks-in-vehicle-platooning.html","line":917},{"title":"MATLAB Sensor Spoofing Video","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/videos/sensor-spoofing-attacks-consequences-and-countermeasures-1550744665433.html","line":918},{"title":"RobustBench: Adversarial Robustness Benchmark","target":"https://robustbench.github.io/","line":919},{"title":"alpha-beta-CROWN Neural Network Verifier","target":"https://github.com/Verified-Intelligence/alpha-beta-CROWN","line":920},{"title":"Gymnasium Classic Control Environments","target":"https://gymnasium.farama.org/environments/classic_control/","line":921},{"title":"TensorFlow FGSM Tutorial","target":"https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials/generative/adversarial_fgsm","line":922},{"title":"PyTorch FGSM Tutorial","target":"https://docs.pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/fgsm_tutorial.html","line":923},{"title":"MIT Underactuated Robotics - Stochastic Systems","target":"https://underactuated.mit.edu/stochastic.html","line":924},{"title":"ONNX Runtime","target":"https://onnxruntime.ai/","line":925},{"title":"ICS Injection Attack Toolbox","target":"https://github.com/sasankapotluri/ICS-Injection_Attack_Toolbox","line":926},{"title":"Adversarial ML Tutorial","target":"https://adversarial-ml-tutorial.org/","line":930},{"title":"MathWorks Adjust Disturbance and Noise Models","target":"https://www.mathworks.com/help/mpc/ug/adjusting-disturbance-and-noise-models.html","line":931},{"title":"Engineering LibreTexts - Noise Modeling","target":"https://eng.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Industrial_and_Systems_Engineering/Chemical_Process_Dynamics_and_Controls_\\(Woolf\\","line":932},{"title":"ScienceDirect - Process Noise Overview","target":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/process-noise","line":933}],"metadata":{"tags":[],"parent":"","collections":[],"This report provides a comprehensive survey of noise models, adversarial attack techniques, simulation frameworks, benchmark problems, and recent research (2023--2026) relevant to defending neural network-based tracking controllers against adversarial attacks. The research covers discrete-time affine-in-the-inputs systems of the form $x(k+1) = f(x(k)) + g(x(k))u(k)$, where neural network controllers compute optimal control inputs and adversarial attacks target sensor measurements, actuator signals, or the neural network itself. Key findings include":"(1) a well-established taxonomy of noise and attack models ranging from Gaussian white noise to sophisticated false data injection and replay attacks; (2) mature simulation toolkits in MATLAB (Robust Control Toolbox, Deep Learning Toolbox, NNV) and Python (ART, Foolbox, python-control); (3) emerging research at the intersection of reinforcement learning, adversarial training, and control-theoretic stability guarantees; and (4) practical IDS/ACC benchmarks directly relevant to this project's analogy framework.","$version":0,"$libraryID":1,"$itemKey":"3ULDQWPF"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[27,33],[37,45],[59,66],[84,90],[100,109],[137,148],[152,161],[165,171],[183,193],[197,204],[228,236],[240,245],[255,258],[278,285],[303,311],[387,391],[413,420],[435,451],[461,467],[490,507],[518,534],[553,564],[574,591]],"last_embed":{"hash":"77pmd4","at":1771186557722}},"smart_blocks:Resources/adversarial-attacks-tracking-control-nn-2026-02-14.md##1. Noise and Disturbance Models for Control Systems (Internal Attack Dynamics)": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.07821813,-0.04827981,0.02501063,0.02428194,-0.00149239,0.02346791,0.02859696,-0.01594046,0.10535698,0.00234378,0.06374608,-0.01156666,0.00456727,0.04784573,-0.01235916,0.07579384,-0.02110185,-0.00533028,-0.00282362,0.04569598,0.06625335,-0.02476541,0.02624101,-0.01748029,0.02923906,-0.00506051,0.00308893,-0.05034785,-0.03837761,-0.24978158,-0.00820325,-0.01219427,0.05487327,0.0121045,-0.01833501,-0.04499707,0.00039652,0.08235467,-0.04882491,0.02296331,0.01003565,0.06373792,0.02752181,-0.04763217,-0.01311088,-0.0582726,-0.05168451,-0.05677003,-0.11617005,-0.05617017,0.00178361,-0.02095028,-0.01180948,-0.06232375,0.02501134,0.0266683,0.09348306,0.03417086,0.0525561,0.0373634,0.02132132,0.03310946,-0.2294011,0.05239059,0.04564525,0.01930636,0.02744162,-0.00583829,0.0237476,-0.00266151,-0.05064973,0.03473722,0.02344723,0.02268011,0.0097321,-0.02538604,0.02805148,-0.05394872,-0.01950781,-0.00849142,0.08111778,0.06447983,-0.02807108,-0.02680366,-0.01160891,0.01592215,-0.00179657,-0.0581944,0.05711982,0.02016431,0.00900844,-0.06074371,0.02427345,0.01694283,0.00908507,-0.00804541,0.03008582,0.02490041,0.0099805,0.06884529,0.02443135,-0.0321145,0.01842793,0.01715626,0.03290286,-0.04162851,-0.04978246,-0.06862479,-0.05734037,-0.00432219,0.01350383,-0.04386674,0.00977308,-0.07728612,0.03522895,-0.04463916,0.02507297,0.03236675,0.00349209,-0.05314765,0.00684658,-0.0185